{"company":{"id":"facebook","name":"Facebook","accent":"#1877f2","asset":"posts","verb":"open the feed"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"App","kind":"client","blurb":"Feed, post, like, profile.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Facebook app on your phone or laptop. Tapping open the feed starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Images and video near the user.","depth":1,"story":"On Facebook, bulky posts are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"api","title":"API gateway","kind":"api","blurb":"Write path and feed reads.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as Facebook’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge posts. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"auth","title":"Identity","kind":"auth","blurb":"Session and graph permissions.","depth":2,"story":"Before Facebook shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"feed","title":"Feed service","kind":"service","blurb":"Assembles the ranked timeline.","depth":2,"story":"Your timeline is assembled and ranked. It is not “dump every post in the world in time order.”"},{"id":"post","title":"Post service","kind":"service","blurb":"Creates a post and kicks fan-out.","depth":2,"story":"Creating a post should feel instant. Telling millions of followers is leftover work on a queue."},{"id":"graph","title":"Social graph","kind":"service","blurb":"Followers / friends.","depth":3,"story":"Who follows whom. Fan-out and privacy both start from this graph."},{"id":"rank","title":"Ranker","kind":"service","blurb":"ML features → order of stories.","depth":3,"story":"Which story is on top. Signals (who you care about, what you watched) — not a random shuffle."},{"id":"cache","title":"Feed cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Precomputed timelines for active users.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Facebook keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"userdb","title":"User DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Profiles and settings.","depth":4,"story":"Your continue-watching / saved list lives here. It is tiny compared with posts, and it is queried often."},{"id":"postdb","title":"Post DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Captions, ids, pointers to media.","depth":4,"story":"This is Facebook’s notebook of records: accounts, titles, orders, messages. Small rows you can query — not the giant posts files."},{"id":"blob","title":"Media store","kind":"blob","blurb":"Original photos and videos.","depth":4,"story":"The warehouse for large posts. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” Facebook points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"queue","title":"Fan-out queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"Push ids to follower inboxes.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at open the feed. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"workers","title":"Fan-out workers","kind":"workers","blurb":"Write to many caches without blocking the poster.","depth":5,"story":"Background helpers at Facebook. They retry if something fails. They are not sitting on the button you just pressed."},{"id":"notify","title":"Notifications","kind":"workers","blurb":"Likes, comments, DMs.","depth":6,"story":"“New episode” or “your driver is here” is a background ping. It is not part of the Play / tap request that already succeeded."},{"id":"search","title":"Search / hashtags","kind":"service","blurb":"Secondary query path.","depth":6,"story":"Find inside files or posts. That is an index, not the warehouse itself."},{"id":"groups","title":"Groups distribution","kind":"service","blurb":"Applies membership and privacy before a group post reaches 